{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"461","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Appleman and Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Appleman has a tree with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices. Some of the vertices (at least one) are colored black and other vertices are colored white."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider a set consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0 ≤ k < n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" edges of Appleman's tree. If Appleman deletes these edges from the tree, then it will split into "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(k + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" parts. Note, that each part will be a tree with colored vertices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Appleman wonders, what is the number of sets splitting the tree in such a way that each resulting part will have exactly one black vertex? Find this number modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2  ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of tree vertices. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains the description of the tree: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p0, p1, ..., pn - 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ pi ≤ i"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" means that there is an edge connecting vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the tree and vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consider tree vertices are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains the description of the colors of the vertices: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x0, x1, ..., xn - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is either "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"). If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" is colored black. Otherwise, vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" is colored white."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — the number of ways to split the tree modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n0 0\n0 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n0 1 1 0 4\n1 1 0 0 1 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n0 1 2 1 4 4 4 0 8\n0 0 0 1 0 1 1 0 0 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"27\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"461B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/461/problem/B"}